[1m[38;5;231mWhich surface needs the logging?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mNode (src/)[39m
     [38;5;246mLog from src/index.js and src/utils.js to stdout/stderr. No transport, no dependency, cheapest to change later.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Browser (app.js)
     [38;5;246mLog from the login flow in app.js. Needs a decision about where logs go and what's safe to record.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Both, shared module
     [38;5;246mOne logging API used by both, with a different sink per runtime. Most work, and the browser risk applies anyway.[39m
